] [17592186553456 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553456 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186553082 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553456 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a97ab0d9-e503-5570-a4f3-0853a9b06c6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553464 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186552938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553464 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553028 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553464 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553137 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553464 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553268 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553464 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553464 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553464 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553464 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186553370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553464 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "baba818e-5aa7-5224-825e-4048b27eb804" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553517 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553448 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553517 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107239" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553517 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553517 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/b8/b892210357f67b41acf4e300f6ec4bc9e78a7c78ceda3c169105c33f02db7f8e.png)\n\nWhat is the name of the polyhedron shown above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553517 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "47178fa5-4a8f-586f-b7df-db62566e23eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553517 #edb/ref 1074 "The polyhedron is a **pentagonal prism** since it has two identical pentagonal faces connected by equal parallel line segments.\n\nAlso, notice that:\n\n- The solid is not a pyramid since a pyramid must have triangular faces (except, possibly, for the base) that meet at a single point.\n\n- The solid is not a rectangular prism since not all of its faces are rectangles." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553541 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553541 #edb/ref 1069 "q-93196" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553541 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553541 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/90/90bdf56a0c09a2db4fae7b19d3625360c4fc148b8807cc3e8a8ba35d1bdf78bb.png)\n\nWhat is the name of the polyhedron shown above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553541 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7e00fa35-b4fc-5e3e-94db-29044e83ec94" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553541 #edb/ref 1074 "The solid is a **heptagonal pyramid** since it is a pyramid whose base is a heptagon.\n\nAlso, notice that:\n\n- The solid is not a heptagonal prism since it has only one heptagonal face.\n\n- The solid is not a hexagonal pyramid since it has no hexagonal face.\n\n- The solid is not a rectangular prism since not all of its faces are rectangles. Due to the same reasons, the solid is not a cube." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553548 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553411 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553548 #edb/ref 1069 "q-117720" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553548 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553548 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is a polyhedron?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553548 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8ad29a00-337d-58d4-9a53-85c6c404f218" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553548 #edb/ref 1074 "Each face in a polyhedron must be a polygon. Therefore, the only option that is a polyhedron is:\n\n![](images/1a/1a04515db528b35af4da3e164522ff54458cba3dee0562e361388860890aa7a7.png)\n\nNotice that all other shapes have at least one face which is not a polygon." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553550 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553550 #edb/ref 1069 "q-117677" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553550 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553550 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/72/729850f1c057d9369a12bec3f1ef006b3c2c097ba6c528fdffe56ccee9eb499a.png)\n\nWhat is the name of the solid shown above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553550 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "92a0b96a-db69-5957-b993-54818494d7c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553550 #edb/ref 1074 "The solid is an **oblique cone**. \n\nNotice the following:\n\n- The solid has one circular base and one vertex. So, it's a cone.\n\n- The axis that passes through the center of the circle and the vertex is not perpendicular to the base. So, it's oblique, not right." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553558 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553558 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61658" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553558 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553558 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/06/063c18aee27eba87852117748b3f90bf75a9785b466516cbf88c01f4300f94e9.png)\n\nWhat is the name of the polyhedron shown above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553558 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9a590bc2-106a-5fb6-90ee-78ac8a96929f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553558 #edb/ref 1074 "The polyhedron is a **pentagonal prism** since it has two identical pentagonal faces connected by equal parallel line segments.\n\nAlso, notice that:\n\n- The solid is not a pyramid since a pyramid must have triangular faces (except, possibly, for the base) that meet at a single point.\n\n- The solid is not a rectangular prism since not all of its faces are rectangles. Due to the same reasons, the solid is not a cube." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553567 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553567 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61643" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553567 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553567 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/71/71c7fda05aab2b4d91df47361b0bbf58f3e65d383a7c4af4e05d27d3e7ea9147.png)\n\nWhat is the name of the polyhedron shown above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553567 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b9f71f42-cce6-5b97-9247-c6bd081ec3db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553567 #edb/ref 1074 "The polyhedron is a **cube** since all its faces are squares.\n\nAlso, notice that:\n\n- The solid is not a pyramid since a pyramid must have triangular faces (except, possibly, for the base).\n\n- The solid is not a triangular prism because it does not have two triangular bases connected by parallel lines." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553575 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553456 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553575 #edb/ref 1069 "q-69864" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553575 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553575 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/81/8144eea23c9f47796eb414502c73044582a3c417abd44684bc4a5cd12d56cfcc.png)\n\nWhat is the name of the polyhedron shown above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553575 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d5776870-d936-568a-a9d6-0ec5e35815ef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553575 #edb/ref 1074 "The polyhedron is a **hexagonal pyramid** since it is a pyramid whose base is a hexagon.  \n\nAlso, notice that:\n\n- The solid is not a rectangular pyramid because it does not have a rectangle as its base.\n\n- The solid is not a triangular pyramid because not all of its faces are triangles.\n\n- The solid is not a hexagonal prism since it has only one hexagonal face.\n\n- The solid is not a rectangular prism since not all of its faces are rectangles." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553581 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553581 #edb/ref 1069 "q-93200" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553581 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553581 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is **not** a polyhedron?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553581 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e13fd4e8-a6eb-59e1-8b7a-96e64d918763" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553581 #edb/ref 1074 "Each face in a polyhedron must be a polygon. Therefore, the only option that is **not** a polyhedron is:\n\n![](images/c3/c392851dd589a891946cbbb17f27164b96c7649abd1f54fbe2a4a943d97e382b.png)\n\nNotice that the top face is not a polygon (it has curved sides)." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
